1
00:00:00,893 --> 00:00:03,393
(We Are in Our Element)

2
00:00:04,263 --> 00:00:07,133
- Nice to see you, everyone. - It's nice to see you all.

3
00:00:07,933 --> 00:00:09,702
Well, is it possible for a TV show...

4
00:00:09,703 --> 00:00:11,942
to get their ratings as high as 9.6 percent these days?

5
00:00:11,943 --> 00:00:13,579
You're suddenly bringing up the TV ratings?

6
00:00:13,603 --> 00:00:15,072
- We just said our greetings. - Well,

7
00:00:15,073 --> 00:00:17,243
- I didn't mean to... - Let us bring that up for you.

8
00:00:18,483 --> 00:00:22,682
(The dutiful son, Moomoo, decided to move to Gimpo, )

9
00:00:22,683 --> 00:00:24,923
(so he could be near his mother.)

10
00:00:25,323 --> 00:00:26,882
Gosh, it will be too far for you.

11
00:00:26,883 --> 00:00:29,392
(He ambitiously went house hunting without telling his mother...)

12
00:00:29,393 --> 00:00:32,623
(to find the dream house for his filial duty.)

13
00:00:32,923 --> 00:00:34,432
You have to move there now.

14
00:00:34,433 --> 00:00:36,662
- He must move. - That's always the conclusion.

15
00:00:36,663 --> 00:00:37,762
Given the results,

16
00:00:37,763 --> 00:00:39,302
I ought to fulfill my filial duty more frequently.

17
00:00:39,303 --> 00:00:41,032
- Right, you must fulfill your duty. - Hyun Moo.

18
00:00:41,033 --> 00:00:42,272
You're going to set the frequency...

19
00:00:42,273 --> 00:00:43,672
- based on the TV ratings? - Seriously.

20
00:00:43,673 --> 00:00:45,913
My mother loves it. She cares about the TV ratings more.

21
00:00:46,103 --> 00:00:47,442
We'll be able to see you being the dutiful son soon.

22
00:00:47,443 --> 00:00:48,572
His segment got high TV ratings.

23
00:00:48,573 --> 00:00:49,943
It will happen within this year.

24
00:00:50,783 --> 00:00:52,689
If I do it too frequently, it won't look sincere.

25
00:00:52,713 --> 00:00:53,782
I'll do it when the weather cools down.

26
00:00:53,783 --> 00:00:54,813
Okay. My gosh.

27
00:00:55,383 --> 00:00:57,853
But I'm happy to see you here.

28
00:00:57,983 --> 00:00:59,082
Everyone said that...

29
00:00:59,083 --> 00:01:00,159
- you wouldn't be on our show. - Right.

30
00:01:00,183 --> 00:01:01,193
- Me? - Yes.

31
00:01:01,553 --> 00:01:04,862
(As he shared the news of his wedding, )

32
00:01:04,863 --> 00:01:07,633
(Jang Woo said goodbye.)

33
00:01:08,233 --> 00:01:11,333
(It made everyone teary-eyed.)

34
00:01:11,633 --> 00:01:13,732
My mother asked me if she should send some flowers.

35
00:01:13,733 --> 00:01:15,372
- Why? - She thought I was done too.

36
00:01:15,373 --> 00:01:16,403
- My gosh. - I see.

37
00:01:16,903 --> 00:01:18,372
- The tears left an impression. - So...

38
00:01:18,373 --> 00:01:20,653
I told her that I could be on the show before my wedding.

39
00:01:20,713 --> 00:01:23,543
We all thought they wouldn't be on the show after the tears.

40
00:01:24,283 --> 00:01:25,782
But they kept joining us including Dae Ho.

41
00:01:25,783 --> 00:01:26,912
Actually, whoever cried...

42
00:01:26,913 --> 00:01:28,452
- came back to the show sooner. - Gosh, of course.

43
00:01:28,453 --> 00:01:29,482
- Right. - Dae Ho...

44
00:01:29,483 --> 00:01:31,283
(That's why I came back sooner.)

45
00:01:32,553 --> 00:01:34,653
(Jang Woo comes out while carrying a heavy bag.)

46
00:01:37,193 --> 00:01:38,293
My gosh. What's that?

47
00:01:38,863 --> 00:01:40,023
(Looking determined)

48
00:01:44,633 --> 00:01:46,233
(Tossing)

49
00:01:48,403 --> 00:01:49,843
- What are you doing? - What's that?

50
00:01:51,303 --> 00:01:52,579
- What's wrong with you? - Is it someone else's bag?

51
00:01:52,603 --> 00:01:53,743
Did you steal it?

52
00:01:56,243 --> 00:01:58,142
- What's he doing? - Did he steal it from someone?

53
00:01:58,143 --> 00:01:59,143
(Joking)

54
00:02:00,583 --> 00:02:01,713
(Ripping)

55
00:02:02,753 --> 00:02:04,553
This looks like the back alley.

56
00:02:04,983 --> 00:02:06,122
Gosh, what's wrong with him?

57
00:02:06,123 --> 00:02:08,083
(He keeps ripping the bag without saying a word.)

58
00:02:08,553 --> 00:02:09,823
Gosh, this looks good.

59
00:02:11,123 --> 00:02:12,493
It looks like a black market deal.

60
00:02:13,863 --> 00:02:15,632
I see. This part here got all rusty.

61
00:02:15,633 --> 00:02:16,763
What's going on? What?

62
00:02:22,273 --> 00:02:24,473
I think I can still use this looking at the condition.

63
00:02:26,603 --> 00:02:28,613
It had the gear for skin and scuba diving.

64
00:02:30,313 --> 00:02:32,283
Skin and scuba diving?

65
00:02:32,413 --> 00:02:33,512
I've neglected them for a long time,

66
00:02:33,513 --> 00:02:35,612
so the zipper was rusted and they were stuck.

67
00:02:35,613 --> 00:02:37,159
How long had it been since your last one?

68
00:02:37,183 --> 00:02:38,453
About 5 to 6 years?

69
00:02:38,853 --> 00:02:40,183
- It had been a while. - Yes.

70
00:02:40,383 --> 00:02:42,453
The marine products are in danger today.

71
00:02:44,423 --> 00:02:46,563
(Dive into Joy)

72
00:02:47,323 --> 00:02:49,793
(He takes out the gear for scuba diving after 7 years.)

73
00:02:50,863 --> 00:02:52,503
I can still use this.

74
00:02:55,273 --> 00:02:59,073
(He rummages through his gear, stirring memories from the past.)

75
00:03:00,603 --> 00:03:03,512
You're going scuba diving today, but look at your gear.

76
00:03:03,513 --> 00:03:04,812
- Right. - Can't you get them repaired?

77
00:03:04,813 --> 00:03:06,759
I could get them repaired. So I decided to take them with me...

78
00:03:06,783 --> 00:03:07,853
and check.

79
00:03:09,253 --> 00:03:11,452
(He loads everything in the car.)

80
00:03:11,453 --> 00:03:13,582
Let's go. Gosh, it's hot.

81
00:03:13,583 --> 00:03:15,293
(He sets off somewhere.)

82
00:03:16,253 --> 00:03:18,263
(He goes scuba diving after 7 years.)

83
00:03:18,823 --> 00:03:22,733
I started skin and scuba diving a long time ago in 2013.

84
00:03:22,863 --> 00:03:26,633
I was completely crazy about it. That was all I did for five years.

85
00:03:26,763 --> 00:03:28,372
When I was young, I loved the sea.

86
00:03:28,373 --> 00:03:29,373
When I was in my 20s,

87
00:03:29,374 --> 00:03:31,372
I used to sit by the water without doing anything special.

88
00:03:31,373 --> 00:03:34,112
- You really love the sea. - I love the sea.

89
00:03:34,113 --> 00:03:36,389
I have the Open Water Diver certification. What do you have?

90
00:03:36,413 --> 00:03:37,712
I'm certified to teach.

91
00:03:37,713 --> 00:03:39,189
(He has the instructor's certificate.)

92
00:03:39,213 --> 00:03:40,242
- I... - Wait, you have a certification?

93
00:03:40,243 --> 00:03:41,952
I do.

94
00:03:41,953 --> 00:03:43,152
But I can only go as low as 20m.

95
00:03:43,153 --> 00:03:44,182
- Why do you have that? - You?

96
00:03:44,183 --> 00:03:46,753
- It was trendy back then. - Open Water, not First in Line?

97
00:03:46,983 --> 00:03:48,699
- I was the first in line for it. - Open Water...

98
00:03:48,723 --> 00:03:49,992
- I always try out everything. - Yes.

99
00:03:49,993 --> 00:03:51,793
(The TSM tries out everything at least once.)

100
00:03:52,363 --> 00:03:54,492
(He loved swimming ever since he was in his 20s.)

101
00:03:54,493 --> 00:03:56,793
Gosh, look how swift he is.

102
00:03:57,663 --> 00:03:59,303
- You can do the butterfly stroke? - Yes.

103
00:03:59,433 --> 00:04:01,032
- Right. A long time ago... - There's our dugong.

104
00:04:01,033 --> 00:04:02,393
(He learned scuba diving in 2013.)

105
00:04:03,303 --> 00:04:05,542
(Underwater has become his favorite place in no time.)

106
00:04:05,543 --> 00:04:07,773
- Gosh, he loves the water. - I do.

107
00:04:08,743 --> 00:04:10,173
(Happy)

108
00:04:12,313 --> 00:04:14,513
- You can also drive yachts now. - Yes.

109
00:04:16,553 --> 00:04:18,182
(Dugong Jang Woo hasn't changed for a long time.)

110
00:04:18,183 --> 00:04:20,153
- He's a great swimmer. - He is.

111
00:04:22,093 --> 00:04:24,923
I did it every day for five years.

112
00:04:25,063 --> 00:04:27,362
You must go diving over 300 times...

113
00:04:27,363 --> 00:04:29,962
- Gosh, 300 times? - to be certified to teach.

114
00:04:29,963 --> 00:04:31,403
Then you become an instructor.

115
00:04:31,863 --> 00:04:33,533
How many hours would 300 dives take?

116
00:04:33,703 --> 00:04:36,373
Naturally, I decided to go for the instructor's certification too.

117
00:04:36,603 --> 00:04:38,272
I got the instructor's certification.

118
00:04:38,273 --> 00:04:41,313
But at one point, I got so busy with work.

119
00:04:41,473 --> 00:04:44,343
I sort of forgot about the romance of just sitting by the sea.

120
00:04:44,513 --> 00:04:47,753
That's when I stopped scuba diving.

121
00:04:48,753 --> 00:04:50,382
That's higher than the advanced certification, right?

122
00:04:50,383 --> 00:04:51,922
- Okay. - I can teach and give people...

123
00:04:51,923 --> 00:04:54,523
- the Open Water certification. - Right. You're an instructor.

124
00:04:54,993 --> 00:04:57,123
- I see. Really? - You can take me along then.

125
00:04:57,323 --> 00:04:59,562
If you can certify someone, it means...

126
00:04:59,563 --> 00:05:01,332
- That's the highest level. - It is.

127
00:05:01,333 --> 00:05:03,253
(The instructor heads to the sea after 7 years.)

128
00:05:03,463 --> 00:05:05,063
It rained so much up until yesterday.

129
00:05:05,563 --> 00:05:07,503
(The weather looks great.)

130
00:05:08,533 --> 00:05:09,602
It's the last...

131
00:05:09,603 --> 00:05:10,672
- of the holiday season. - Right. It's no joke.

132
00:05:10,673 --> 00:05:11,873
Gosh, there are so many cars.

133
00:05:11,973 --> 00:05:13,873
(But he can't conceal his excitement.)

134
00:05:15,473 --> 00:05:17,043
But it must be fun there.

135
00:05:17,143 --> 00:05:18,213
It's great.

136
00:05:18,443 --> 00:05:20,163
Yes, Gangwon Province is the perfect place.

137
00:05:20,483 --> 00:05:21,982
(Goseong)

138
00:05:21,983 --> 00:05:23,213
- Goseong. - Goseong.

139
00:05:24,953 --> 00:05:26,053
It's the sea.

140
00:05:26,983 --> 00:05:28,052
It's the sea.

141
00:05:28,053 --> 00:05:29,599
(The blue ocean stretches out before his eyes.)

142
00:05:29,623 --> 00:05:30,793
Gosh, it's been a long time.

143
00:05:31,763 --> 00:05:33,393
I'm finally here.

144
00:05:35,533 --> 00:05:37,062
What? There are so many people.

145
00:05:37,063 --> 00:05:40,503
It's located by the Ayajin Beach of Goseong in Gangwon Province.

146
00:05:40,633 --> 00:05:41,672
I went to...

147
00:05:41,673 --> 00:05:43,602
- a skin and scuba diving shop. - Ayajin Beach.

148
00:05:43,603 --> 00:05:45,942
(A clean-water spot at the edge of Gangwon Province)

149
00:05:45,943 --> 00:05:47,043
(Ayajin Beach)

150
00:05:47,473 --> 00:05:49,573
(The clear water and clean sandy beach...)

151
00:05:50,773 --> 00:05:52,082
- Goseong and Gangneung... - It's in Goseong.

152
00:05:52,083 --> 00:05:53,483
- are trending these days. - Right.

153
00:05:54,753 --> 00:05:56,783
Hello.

154
00:05:57,153 --> 00:05:58,223
Hello.

155
00:05:59,523 --> 00:06:01,352
Hello. Did you already go for a dive?

156
00:06:01,353 --> 00:06:02,393
Yes.

157
00:06:02,823 --> 00:06:03,852
- Hello. - Jang Woo!

158
00:06:03,853 --> 00:06:05,563
- Hey! Hello. - Jang Woo, it's hot today.

159
00:06:06,423 --> 00:06:07,462
- Hello. - Jang Woo!

160
00:06:07,463 --> 00:06:09,393
- Hey! Hello. - Jang Woo, it's hot today.

161
00:06:09,533 --> 00:06:10,662
- Who's that? - You sound like you know her.

162
00:06:10,663 --> 00:06:12,562
- It's so hot today. - Did you already go for a dive?

163
00:06:12,563 --> 00:06:14,372
No, not me. I have customers here.

164
00:06:14,373 --> 00:06:15,503
- Gosh. - Really?

165
00:06:16,773 --> 00:06:17,843
You!

166
00:06:18,903 --> 00:06:20,143
How dare he fire me?

167
00:06:20,373 --> 00:06:25,283
(She was in dramas such as "Pasta" and "My Too Perfect Sons.")

168
00:06:26,083 --> 00:06:27,083
(She established herself as the scene-stealer.)

169
00:06:27,084 --> 00:06:28,583
My gosh. That was a long time ago.

170
00:06:29,413 --> 00:06:31,553
Jae Suk is my senior actress.

171
00:06:31,653 --> 00:06:34,223
She and I got the Open Water Diver certification together.

172
00:06:34,323 --> 00:06:37,052
We practiced in the swimming pool and told ourselves we'd go to Jeju.

173
00:06:37,053 --> 00:06:38,663
So we did go to Jeju Island together...

174
00:06:38,863 --> 00:06:40,392
and went for our first dive.

175
00:06:40,393 --> 00:06:42,462
Afterward, we were together every day for several years.

176
00:06:42,463 --> 00:06:43,632
We did that for years together.

177
00:06:43,633 --> 00:06:44,762
I'd call her up and ask, "Should we?"

178
00:06:44,763 --> 00:06:46,233
Then we went to the sea.

179
00:06:46,403 --> 00:06:48,172
We didn't even book a room or anything.

180
00:06:48,173 --> 00:06:50,502
We slept for a bit in the car and went for a dive.

181
00:06:50,503 --> 00:06:51,902
- You were serious about it. - We floated around on the ocean...

182
00:06:51,903 --> 00:06:53,303
for five hours and had fun.

183
00:06:54,373 --> 00:06:56,772
We were just floating around the water, but we loved that.

184
00:06:56,773 --> 00:06:57,782
(They were just happy to be on the water all day.)

185
00:06:57,783 --> 00:06:59,443
We did that every day.

186
00:07:00,313 --> 00:07:02,982
Everyone said that I was literally crazy about the ocean.

187
00:07:02,983 --> 00:07:03,983
That's how much I loved it.

188
00:07:03,984 --> 00:07:05,122
When I asked if she was going for a dive,

189
00:07:05,123 --> 00:07:06,282
she'd say we should go to the Ayajin Beach.

190
00:07:06,283 --> 00:07:07,992
That was like our rule.

191
00:07:07,993 --> 00:07:09,152
I asked to go somewhere else.

192
00:07:09,153 --> 00:07:10,469
But she always chose the Ayajin Beach.

193
00:07:10,493 --> 00:07:13,763
So we ended up coming here every single time.

194
00:07:14,023 --> 00:07:15,163
- Sir! - Hey.

195
00:07:16,063 --> 00:07:17,193
- Sir! - Hey.

196
00:07:17,763 --> 00:07:19,403
- My gear... - Yes.

197
00:07:19,563 --> 00:07:22,573
That's her husband. He's totally the man of the ocean.

198
00:07:24,073 --> 00:07:25,642
It's been so long.

199
00:07:25,643 --> 00:07:28,473
I couldn't even zip it open, so I had to cut it.

200
00:07:29,113 --> 00:07:31,082
I had to cut it open. They were all rusted.

201
00:07:31,083 --> 00:07:32,382
I can still use this, right?

202
00:07:32,383 --> 00:07:34,553
- Gosh, it's been a long time. - Yes, it has.

203
00:07:34,683 --> 00:07:35,852
This won't be easy. You know?

204
00:07:35,853 --> 00:07:37,752
Will I be able to fit into any suit?

205
00:07:37,753 --> 00:07:39,723
- The dry suit won't fit, right? - The dry suit?

206
00:07:39,883 --> 00:07:41,123
It doesn't fit me either!

207
00:07:41,523 --> 00:07:43,422
- I can't even put my feet in it. - Right.

208
00:07:43,423 --> 00:07:44,762
Same here. It gets stuck on my feet.

209
00:07:44,763 --> 00:07:45,892
Not even my feet.

210
00:07:45,893 --> 00:07:47,063
I wonder if this will fit.

211
00:07:47,423 --> 00:07:48,592
- Gosh. - Give him a big one.

212
00:07:48,593 --> 00:07:49,733
It's been a while.

213
00:07:50,393 --> 00:07:52,003
Jang Woo, try that one on.

214
00:07:52,403 --> 00:07:53,503
Thank you.

215
00:07:54,003 --> 00:07:55,532
- Let me get changed. - You should get changed too, honey.

216
00:07:55,533 --> 00:07:56,533
(Let me give it a try.)

217
00:07:57,203 --> 00:07:58,363
I wonder if this will fit me.

218
00:07:59,473 --> 00:08:02,312
(Struggling)

219
00:08:02,313 --> 00:08:03,612
(Screaming)

220
00:08:03,613 --> 00:08:04,613
(Panting)

221
00:08:05,413 --> 00:08:06,642
Gosh, it won't fit.

222
00:08:06,643 --> 00:08:08,182
- It won't fit. He will rip it. - It won't fit.

223
00:08:08,183 --> 00:08:10,059
- Did you put it on? - Were you able to wear it?

224
00:08:10,083 --> 00:08:11,183
Did you put it on?

225
00:08:11,883 --> 00:08:13,053
- Gosh. - Oh, my. Hey.

226
00:08:14,793 --> 00:08:16,352
(Looking towering)

227
00:08:16,353 --> 00:08:18,473
- I think he lost some weight. - They're like tights.

228
00:08:18,723 --> 00:08:20,263
(What do you think?)

229
00:08:20,523 --> 00:08:22,233
Can you move around in it? That's good.

230
00:08:22,533 --> 00:08:23,593
What a relief.

231
00:08:24,633 --> 00:08:25,862
This looks good, right?

232
00:08:25,863 --> 00:08:26,963
Jae Suk. Right?

233
00:08:27,873 --> 00:08:28,873
You look cute.

234
00:08:28,874 --> 00:08:30,409
- Why do you look so cute? - Why are you wet?

235
00:08:30,433 --> 00:08:31,472
- I had a hard time putting it on. - Isn't that too long?

236
00:08:31,473 --> 00:08:32,543
I sprayed water.

237
00:08:34,043 --> 00:08:35,742
The fishing village chief heard you were coming...

238
00:08:35,743 --> 00:08:37,442
and dropped off some whelks.

239
00:08:37,443 --> 00:08:39,042
- Really? - So I could eat them with you.

240
00:08:39,043 --> 00:08:40,243
The president of the sea.

241
00:08:40,483 --> 00:08:42,712
The chief also gave us some squids he had caught.

242
00:08:42,713 --> 00:08:44,453
- Just regular squids? - The live ones.

243
00:08:45,383 --> 00:08:47,522
(I love it.)

244
00:08:47,523 --> 00:08:49,853
- He's loving it. - Let's go for a short dive...

245
00:08:50,353 --> 00:08:51,523
and enjoy a long night.

246
00:08:51,893 --> 00:08:53,693
- It's so hot. - Wipe your face with a towel.

247
00:08:54,993 --> 00:08:56,363
Here you go. Wipe your face.

248
00:08:56,933 --> 00:09:00,433
Before we set sail, we need to prepare the life jackets.

249
00:09:00,803 --> 00:09:02,202
- I'll bring them right away. - Okay.

250
00:09:02,203 --> 00:09:03,403
Wet your face too.

251
00:09:03,503 --> 00:09:04,673
- Did you do it? - I did it.

252
00:09:05,943 --> 00:09:07,043
I'll be back.

253
00:09:07,443 --> 00:09:09,373
- Jang Woo, did you eat? - No.

254
00:09:09,573 --> 00:09:11,442
- Don't you get seasick? - I don't get seasick at all.

255
00:09:11,443 --> 00:09:12,613
- Not at all? - No.

