1278
00:48:12,097 --> 00:48:13,137
Gosh!

1279
00:48:15,967 --> 00:48:17,036
It's the squid ramyeon.

1280
00:48:17,037 --> 00:48:18,037
(Dreams come true.)

1281
00:48:18,837 --> 00:48:20,446
Gosh! Stop it.

1282
00:48:20,447 --> 00:48:22,747
So you can pick that much food with chopsticks.

1283
00:48:24,447 --> 00:48:26,016
As the ramyeon was boiled in the squid broth,

1284
00:48:26,017 --> 00:48:27,746
- It tastes totally different. - the noodles didn't get soggy.

1285
00:48:27,747 --> 00:48:29,687
- You're right. - The noodles are chewy.

1286
00:48:31,217 --> 00:48:32,986
(Jae Suk takes a bite of the chewy squid ramyeon too.)

1287
00:48:32,987 --> 00:48:34,927
- Gosh. - This is how it should be cooked.

1288
00:48:35,687 --> 00:48:37,426
- This is how it should be cooked. - Gosh.

1289
00:48:37,427 --> 00:48:39,196
- Gosh, I'm so jealous. - They really look like siblings.

1290
00:48:39,197 --> 00:48:40,703
(The Dugong Siblings eat just like each other too.)

1291
00:48:40,727 --> 00:48:41,896
I will experience a bit of extravagance.

1292
00:48:41,897 --> 00:48:43,367
- Go ahead. - Eat all you want.

1293
00:48:44,167 --> 00:48:46,037
There's another bowl if you need more.

1294
00:48:46,097 --> 00:48:48,177
The sea urchin roe was placed on top of the ramyeon.

1295
00:48:48,237 --> 00:48:50,536
- Gosh. - That's unbelievable.

1296
00:48:50,537 --> 00:48:51,857
Placing it on top of the ramyeon?

1297
00:48:51,977 --> 00:48:52,977
(Slurping)

1298
00:48:54,407 --> 00:48:57,517
(He tastes the extravagance with his eyes closed.)

1299
00:48:58,777 --> 00:49:00,316
(Amazed)

1300
00:49:00,317 --> 00:49:01,387
Cheese ramyeon.

1301
00:49:02,247 --> 00:49:03,956
It became just like cheese ramyeon right away.

1302
00:49:03,957 --> 00:49:05,833
(Clean and savory sea urchin roe just like cheese)

1303
00:49:05,857 --> 00:49:07,356
I don't think you will gain any weight with food like this.

1304
00:49:07,357 --> 00:49:08,677
You're wrong. You do gain weight.

1305
00:49:08,957 --> 00:49:10,126
You'll be in big trouble if you think that way.

1306
00:49:10,127 --> 00:49:12,097
I gained so much weight after coming here.

1307
00:49:14,727 --> 00:49:16,266
(Taking a bite of the steamed squid after being ready to gain weight)

1308
00:49:16,267 --> 00:49:17,496
My gosh.

1309
00:49:17,497 --> 00:49:19,673
(Taking a bite of the steamed squid after being ready to gain weight)

1310
00:49:19,697 --> 00:49:20,707
(Satisfied)

1311
00:49:21,307 --> 00:49:22,307
It's so savory.

1312
00:49:22,737 --> 00:49:23,877
Right.

1313
00:49:24,977 --> 00:49:26,176
This tastes like crab innards.

1314
00:49:26,177 --> 00:49:28,147
(The squid innards taste like crab innards.)

1315
00:49:28,277 --> 00:49:29,977
That can be eaten only when it's fresh.

1316
00:49:32,247 --> 00:49:33,886
(Freshness spread inside his whole mouth)

1317
00:49:33,887 --> 00:49:35,017
You should have it.

1318
00:49:35,647 --> 00:49:37,116
(Sweating)

1319
00:49:37,117 --> 00:49:38,797
There's so much broth coming out from him.

1320
00:49:39,827 --> 00:49:40,987
It was really tender.

1321
00:49:41,327 --> 00:49:43,397
It was full of flavor...

1322
00:49:43,727 --> 00:49:45,127
and it had the saltiness of salt.

1323
00:49:45,597 --> 00:49:47,127
(Letting out a breath for the squid)

1324
00:49:47,997 --> 00:49:49,837
(Just like the younger Dugong that is happy, )

1325
00:49:50,697 --> 00:49:53,467
(the older Dugong targets the squid.)

1326
00:49:54,707 --> 00:49:56,066
So it's eaten without any chojang.

1327
00:49:56,067 --> 00:49:57,977
There was no need for any.

1328
00:50:00,177 --> 00:50:01,507
We have squid all the time,

1329
00:50:01,877 --> 00:50:03,437
but I keep wanting to have the jjajang.

1330
00:50:03,847 --> 00:50:05,576
- The jjajang is good, isn't it? - Would you like some more?

1331
00:50:05,577 --> 00:50:07,147
You should have it. I'm okay.

1332
00:50:07,387 --> 00:50:09,647
My gosh.

1333
00:50:10,217 --> 00:50:11,256
We finished it already.

1334
00:50:11,257 --> 00:50:12,356
(Finishing a bowl of jjajang in a flash)

1335
00:50:12,357 --> 00:50:13,857
Gosh, it was finished already.

1336
00:50:13,987 --> 00:50:15,887
(Satisfied)

1337
00:50:16,427 --> 00:50:18,196
You should eat a lot. You have work tomorrow.

1338
00:50:18,197 --> 00:50:19,197
It'll be tough.

1339
00:50:20,667 --> 00:50:23,127
(Astonished)

1340
00:50:23,737 --> 00:50:24,766
Hold on.

1341
00:50:24,767 --> 00:50:27,136
(He gets up.)

1342
00:50:27,137 --> 00:50:28,166
By the seawall.

1343
00:50:28,167 --> 00:50:29,807
- What's that? - What is it?

1344
00:50:30,177 --> 00:50:31,653
What? Why did you get something so expensive?

1345
00:50:31,677 --> 00:50:32,876
- Is it from Seoul? - I can't tell who these are for.

1346
00:50:32,877 --> 00:50:34,907
- "Is it from Seoul?" - "Is it from Seoul?"

1347
00:50:35,247 --> 00:50:36,746
The big one should be for me.

1348
00:50:36,747 --> 00:50:37,817
No.

1349
00:50:38,077 --> 00:50:39,116
- Here you are. - Thank you.

1350
00:50:39,117 --> 00:50:41,386
Gosh, he's so caring.

1351
00:50:41,387 --> 00:50:42,387
(Feeling proud)

1352
00:50:43,417 --> 00:50:44,656
They're matching.

1353
00:50:44,657 --> 00:50:46,086
- It's perfect. - Right.

1354
00:50:46,087 --> 00:50:48,756
I saw it, and it reminded me of him right away.

1355
00:50:48,757 --> 00:50:50,226
Right. It looks great.

1356
00:50:50,227 --> 00:50:51,227
It's perfect for him.

1357
00:50:51,228 --> 00:50:52,326
- That's a smart gift. - It's cute.

1358
00:50:52,327 --> 00:50:53,866
- Thank you. - Gosh, you don't need to thank me.

1359
00:50:53,867 --> 00:50:55,627
We should use them when we go to the valley.

1360
00:50:55,967 --> 00:50:56,967
(Feeling proud)

1361
00:50:56,968 --> 00:50:58,896
Gosh, we should eat more.

1362
00:50:58,897 --> 00:51:00,737
(We should eat more as we feel great.)

1363
00:51:01,607 --> 00:51:02,736
I finished the jjajang.

1364
00:51:02,737 --> 00:51:03,737
(Eating the octopus too)

1365
00:51:04,207 --> 00:51:05,277
It's so good.

1366
00:51:05,607 --> 00:51:07,076
It's been a while since I've seen you...

1367
00:51:07,077 --> 00:51:08,106
and you're still the same.

1368
00:51:08,107 --> 00:51:09,477
The same goes for you.

1369
00:51:09,547 --> 00:51:12,347
You two are eating and seeing great things together,

1370
00:51:12,747 --> 00:51:14,346
- so you haven't aged. - What are you saying?

1371
00:51:14,347 --> 00:51:16,046
We're soon going to turn 50.

1372
00:51:16,047 --> 00:51:17,617
We're almost 50.

1373
00:51:17,987 --> 00:51:20,127
- Were you that old? - Yes. I was born in 1979.

1374
00:51:20,557 --> 00:51:21,787
I'm from the Class of 2001.

1375
00:51:22,187 --> 00:51:23,456
- What? - She's the same as me.

1376
00:51:23,457 --> 00:51:24,927
- She looks really young. - Right.

1377
00:51:25,357 --> 00:51:26,697
I'm from the Class of 2009.

1378
00:51:26,897 --> 00:51:27,996
Were you born in 1986?

1379
00:51:27,997 --> 00:51:29,096
I told you.

1380
00:51:29,097 --> 00:51:31,366
Why did I think that you were around my age?

1381
00:51:31,367 --> 00:51:32,367
I thought that too.

1382
00:51:32,368 --> 00:51:34,536
It's because we hang out in similar ways.

1383
00:51:34,537 --> 00:51:35,783
- We enjoy similar things. - Right.

1384
00:51:35,807 --> 00:51:37,927
I really thought he wasn't that much younger than me.

1385
00:51:38,007 --> 00:51:39,606
- I had no idea. - I'm still 40 now.

1386
00:51:39,607 --> 00:51:40,847
(I'm still 40 now.)

1387
00:51:41,007 --> 00:51:42,707
Gosh, I saw him when he was in his 20s.

1388
00:51:42,947 --> 00:51:44,647
It's time for you to ripen now.

1389
00:51:44,877 --> 00:51:46,476
- I've ripened a lot. - Right.

1390
00:51:46,477 --> 00:51:47,816
(I've ripened a lot.)

1391
00:51:47,817 --> 00:51:49,017
He has ripened.

1392
00:51:50,257 --> 00:51:52,417
Lost in the fantasy alone.

1393
00:51:52,817 --> 00:51:55,287
We made spicy seafood stew with all of the people around.

1394
00:51:55,687 --> 00:51:56,826
I went around a lot with Jang Woo.

1395
00:51:56,827 --> 00:51:58,056
- We went to Tae Island too. - Right.

1396
00:51:58,057 --> 00:51:59,617
- We went to a lot of islands. - Right.

1397
00:52:00,067 --> 00:52:01,967
I'm quite certain about this.

1398
00:52:02,627 --> 00:52:04,137
The sea to me is my 20s.

1399
00:52:04,937 --> 00:52:06,657
- It's your youth. - My memories of my 20s.

1400
00:52:07,907 --> 00:52:10,906
My car, camping gear, and everything I had...

1401
00:52:10,907 --> 00:52:14,577
was focused on the sea.

1402
00:52:15,007 --> 00:52:16,647
That was how close I lived to the sea.

1403
00:52:16,847 --> 00:52:17,947
That's impressive.

1404
00:52:18,217 --> 00:52:19,617
I was really crazy about the sea.

1405
00:52:20,147 --> 00:52:21,717
As I age year after year,

1406
00:52:22,347 --> 00:52:25,856
I live the same way I live...

1407
00:52:25,857 --> 00:52:27,957
when I work or meet people.

1408
00:52:28,627 --> 00:52:30,657
But as I received this great energy today,

1409
00:52:31,757 --> 00:52:34,627
something that was stuck inside my head got relieved.

1410
00:52:35,097 --> 00:52:36,866
I was able to revisit my memories of my 20s...

1411
00:52:36,867 --> 00:52:40,907
and learn how to be humble before the sea.

1412
00:52:41,407 --> 00:52:42,507
It was great.

1413
00:52:42,807 --> 00:52:43,807
The abalone is this big!

1414
00:52:43,808 --> 00:52:46,507
The sea didn't change at all. I should visit more often.

1415
00:52:48,777 --> 00:52:49,847
Right!

1416
00:52:52,017 --> 00:52:55,346
(The Sea Here Again)

1417
00:52:55,347 --> 00:52:56,417
(I Live Alone)

1418
00:52:56,817 --> 00:52:59,817
(The Link Between You and Me)

1419
00:53:00,457 --> 00:53:01,586
(Is Ju Seung heading somewhere?)

1420
00:53:01,587 --> 00:53:03,327
Gosh, you're wearing a dress shirt.

1421
00:53:03,597 --> 00:53:05,477
It had been a while since I had an appointment.

1422
00:53:06,727 --> 00:53:07,867
Gosh, so this is it.

1423
00:53:08,967 --> 00:53:09,997
It's big.

1424
00:53:12,637 --> 00:53:13,637
(Peeking)

1425
00:53:14,407 --> 00:53:15,606
- Where are you going? - Where is this place?

1426
00:53:15,607 --> 00:53:16,906
It's the Brachiosaurus.

1427
00:53:16,907 --> 00:53:18,387
- "Brachiosaurus?" - All of a sudden?

1428
00:53:19,077 --> 00:53:20,177
What's this one?

1429
00:53:21,447 --> 00:53:22,447
(Natural history museum?)

1430
00:53:22,448 --> 00:53:23,916
- Seodaemun? - There's a place like this...

1431
00:53:23,917 --> 00:53:24,976
in Seodaemun?

1432
00:53:24,977 --> 00:53:26,076
This would be really scary to meet.

1433
00:53:26,077 --> 00:53:28,357
(A vicious creature protects the natural history museum.)

1434
00:53:28,517 --> 00:53:30,387
(Looking intently)

1435
00:53:30,717 --> 00:53:32,357
I would faint if I actually saw this.

1436
00:53:33,057 --> 00:53:35,187
I was always very interested in dinosaurs.

1437
00:53:35,557 --> 00:53:37,656
The new series of "Jurassic Park" was released,

1438
00:53:37,657 --> 00:53:40,126
so I went to watch it. I ended up falling for them even more.

1439
00:53:40,127 --> 00:53:43,267
I recently got invited to a film festival in Dallas...

1440
00:53:43,467 --> 00:53:45,667
and that was why I went to the US.

1441
00:53:45,797 --> 00:53:47,466
There was a natural history museum there...

1442
00:53:47,467 --> 00:53:48,536
and it was really big.

1443
00:53:48,537 --> 00:53:50,577
- It does look really big behind. - It's massive.

1444
00:53:50,707 --> 00:53:52,577
They actually dig out fossils there.

1445
00:53:52,637 --> 00:53:53,706
- Really? - Yes.

1446
00:53:53,707 --> 00:53:55,446
You can see people digging fossils out behind glass walls.

1447
00:53:55,447 --> 00:53:57,087
The place that appeared in "I Am Museum?"

1448
00:53:57,747 --> 00:53:58,816
"Night at the Museum."

1449
00:53:58,817 --> 00:54:00,316
- Oh, right. - "I Am Museum?"

1450
00:54:00,317 --> 00:54:01,646
What's "I Am Museum?"

1451
00:54:01,647 --> 00:54:02,816
That's "I Am a Natural Person..."

1452
00:54:02,817 --> 00:54:04,256
and "Night at the Museum" mixed together.

1453
00:54:04,257 --> 00:54:06,617
I like movies that start with "I am."

1454
00:54:07,327 --> 00:54:09,526
- "I Am Museum." - It sounds like a documentary.

1455
00:54:09,527 --> 00:54:10,997
I was totally mesmerized.

1456
00:54:11,357 --> 00:54:14,097
I wondered if there was one in Korea and found this place.

1457
00:54:15,127 --> 00:54:16,607
There was a place like this in Korea?

1458
00:54:17,137 --> 00:54:18,437
So I have to line up here.

1459
00:54:19,037 --> 00:54:21,197
This place is really popular even during the weekdays.

1460
00:54:24,607 --> 00:54:26,107
- Hello. - Hello.

1461
00:54:27,277 --> 00:54:29,507
- One ticket, please. - Right.

1462
00:54:30,177 --> 00:54:32,376
It's Culture Day today, so you get a 20 percent discount.

1463
00:54:32,377 --> 00:54:33,447
- Oh, right. - Yes.

1464
00:54:33,817 --> 00:54:35,487
You look much better in person.

1465
00:54:35,717 --> 00:54:36,757
Thank you.

1466
00:54:36,817 --> 00:54:37,986
She offers lip service to him too.

1467
00:54:37,987 --> 00:54:40,156
(Joking)

1468
00:54:40,157 --> 00:54:41,157
(Beeping)

1469
00:54:41,158 --> 00:54:43,318
(He pleasantly enters the museum with the compliment.)

1470
00:54:45,997 --> 00:54:47,067
Amazing.

1471
00:54:47,267 --> 00:54:48,667
Gosh, it's big.

1472
00:54:49,427 --> 00:54:51,066
(It's grand.)

1473
00:54:51,067 --> 00:54:52,337
(Eyes opening wide)

1474
00:54:54,667 --> 00:54:57,707
(An overwhelming sight)

1475
00:54:59,577 --> 00:55:01,046
(The dinosaurs Ju Seung wished to see are all gathered.)

1476
00:55:01,047 --> 00:55:02,247
It's set up really well.

1477
00:55:04,117 --> 00:55:05,376
That's the headbutting dinosaur.

1478
00:55:05,377 --> 00:55:07,587
- The Pachycephalosaurus. - Right.

1479
00:55:08,047 --> 00:55:10,317
I heard that its skull was 20cm thick.

1480
00:55:10,917 --> 00:55:13,156
(He greets the massive dinosaur bones.)

1481
00:55:13,157 --> 00:55:15,057
That's the Acrocanthosaurus.

1482
00:55:15,287 --> 00:55:18,127
It means it's a lizard with tall neural spine sails.

1483
00:55:18,697 --> 00:55:20,527
- You know a lot. - It's a theropod.

1484
00:55:20,727 --> 00:55:21,927
There are saurischians...

1485
00:55:22,127 --> 00:55:23,637
- Saurischians? - and ornithischians.

1486
00:55:24,067 --> 00:55:25,566
Under the saurischians,

1487
00:55:25,567 --> 00:55:28,267
there are theropods and sauropods.

1488
00:55:28,807 --> 00:55:31,306
Do you know what "dinosaur" means?

1489
00:55:31,307 --> 00:55:33,337
(Do you know what "dinosaur" means?)

1490
00:55:33,677 --> 00:55:34,806
- "Dinosaur?" - "Dinosaur?"

1491
00:55:34,807 --> 00:55:35,807
- "Dinosaur?" - I don't have a clue.

1492
00:55:35,808 --> 00:55:37,276
- "Dinosaur?" - Doesn't "saur" mean "lizard?"

1493
00:55:37,277 --> 00:55:38,416
- Right. - Right.

1494
00:55:38,417 --> 00:55:39,577
Is it "scary lizard?"

1495
00:55:40,017 --> 00:55:41,117
- You're right. - What?

1496
00:55:41,717 --> 00:55:43,387
- What? - Really?

1497
00:55:43,987 --> 00:55:45,016
(He got this right?)

1498
00:55:45,017 --> 00:55:46,386
- Congratulations. - Nice one.

1499
00:55:46,387 --> 00:55:47,787
(Moomoo gets it right.)

1500
00:55:47,927 --> 00:55:49,756
"Dino" means "scary."

1501
00:55:49,757 --> 00:55:50,757
- Right. - "Saur" means "lizard."

1502
00:55:50,758 --> 00:55:52,396
- I see. - "Scary lizard."

1503
00:55:52,397 --> 00:55:53,917
Did you know that birds are dinosaurs?

1504
00:55:54,527 --> 00:55:55,566
Pterosaurs.

1505
00:55:55,567 --> 00:55:57,367
- All birds? - All birds.

1506
00:55:57,697 --> 00:55:58,736
- Right. - Even sparrows...

1507
00:55:58,737 --> 00:55:59,737
- and pigeons. - Even chicks?

1508
00:55:59,737 --> 00:56:00,737
- They're all dinosaurs? - Yes.

1509
00:56:00,738 --> 00:56:02,043
Are they descendants of Pterosaurs?

1510
00:56:02,067 --> 00:56:03,907
No. Pterosaurs aren't dinosaurs.

1511
00:56:04,307 --> 00:56:06,407
- Pterosaurs aren't dinosaurs? - They're different.

1512
00:56:06,677 --> 00:56:07,707
Really?

1513
00:56:08,907 --> 00:56:10,277
It's massive in scale.

1514
00:56:10,817 --> 00:56:11,847
It's fascinating.

1515
00:56:12,117 --> 00:56:14,846
We were constantly exposed to them starting from a young age...

1516
00:56:14,847 --> 00:56:17,657
and it didn't feel that fascinating.

1517
00:56:17,887 --> 00:56:20,287
There are actually a lot of fascinating creatures around us.

1518
00:56:20,687 --> 00:56:24,257
Giraffes have long necks.

1519
00:56:24,757 --> 00:56:26,427
Lions and tigers are fascinating too.

1520
00:56:26,797 --> 00:56:30,027
But dinosaurs were even more fascinating.

1521
00:56:30,597 --> 00:56:32,997
There was a creature that was 80t.

1522
00:56:33,667 --> 00:56:36,137
The bite force of the Tyrannosauros...

1523
00:56:36,267 --> 00:56:40,137
is strong enough to bring down an elephant.

1524
00:56:40,577 --> 00:56:41,846
- Gosh. - How would it be...

1525
00:56:41,847 --> 00:56:43,047
if they were still alive?

1526
00:56:43,577 --> 00:56:45,517
This is the Argentinosauros.

1527
00:56:45,917 --> 00:56:48,987
It's the tallest and biggest dinosaur.

1528
00:56:49,147 --> 00:56:50,457
The Tyrannosaurus is this big.

1529
00:56:53,087 --> 00:56:54,356
That's a big difference.

1530
00:56:54,357 --> 00:56:55,903
The Argentinosauros is 11 times heavier.

1531
00:56:55,927 --> 00:56:58,127
It must've been like a lion fighting against a giraffe.

1532
00:56:58,357 --> 00:57:00,037
No matter how strong the Tyrannosaurus is,

